@startuml
'https://plantuml.com/class-diagram
!theme spacelab

title Communication Client Core — Protocol-Neutral Point Model

interface PointAddress<T> {
}
note right of PointAddress
  Opaque handle to a single addressable
  value of type T (e.g. Boolean, Integer,
  Duration, a vendor-defined enum, ...).
  Callers never inspect its contents.
  Concrete meaning (register, coil, tag,
  object-id, ...) is defined entirely by
  whichever protocol adapter created it.
end note

interface PointSnapshot {
  +<T> valueOf(point: PointAddress<T>): Response<T>
}
note right of PointSnapshot
  Read result keyed by the PointAddress
  instances that were requested.
end note

interface CommunicationClient {
  +connect(): CompletableFuture<Response<Void>>
  +disconnect(): void
  +isConnected(): boolean
  +read(points: List<PointAddress<?>>): CompletableFuture<Response<PointSnapshot>>
  +<T> write(point: PointAddress<T>, value: T): CompletableFuture<Response<Void>>
}
note right of CommunicationClient
  The ONLY communication API the rest of the
  system sees. Devices talk in points and
  values only — no protocol vocabulary
  (registers, coils, tags, ...) appears here,
  regardless of which protocol is used
  underneath.
end note

class Response<T> {
  +status: Status
  +details: String
  +value: T
}

enum Status {
  OK
  EXCEPTION
}

CommunicationClient ..> PointAddress : reads/writes
CommunicationClient ..> PointSnapshot : returns from read
CommunicationClient ..> Response : returns
Response -- Status

note bottom of CommunicationClient
  How a CommunicationClient is created and
  configured is covered in 02 Connection
  Provisioning. How Modbus implements this
  port is covered in 03 Modbus Adapter.
end note

@enduml
